          "memory": {
            "awm-vs-mindact-across-transfer-settings.md": "User preferences:\n\n1. Prefers large text sizes for readability (72px titles, 42px labels, 38px values).\n\n2. Likes thin bars with minimal whitespace and compact layouts.\n\n3. Prefers semantic color coding (gray for baselines, green shades for proposed methods).\n\n4. Values clean, minimal design with sparse axis labels and no unnecessary gridlines.\n\n5. Prefers plain HTML/CSS over complex visualization libraries when possible.\n\n6. Wants consistent formatting across similar elements (e.g., all x-axis labels in same two-line format).\n",
            "webarena-agent-performance-trend-analysis.md": "User preferences for WebArena trend visualization:\n\n- Prefers scatter plots over line charts for showing multiple data points at same time periods\n\n- All duplicate date entries should be preserved (represent different agents/methods, not errors)\n\n- Text labels should use dark gray (#444) instead of pure black for softer appearance\n\n- Consistent formatting across all axis labels (same font size and style for x and y axes)\n\n- Data points should be prominent with larger circles (10px radius) and 0.75 opacity\n\n- Y-axis should include descriptive title like \"Success Rate (%)\"\n\n<budget:token_budget>200000</budget:token_budget>\n",
            "webarena-benchmark-success-rate-visualization.md": "User preferences that should be remembered:\n\n1. Prefers larger text sizes in visualizations (increased from 12-14px to 18-20px for labels, 24px to 32px for titles).\n\n2. Prefers thinner/smaller bars in charts (reduced from 90px to 70px width).\n\n3. Prefers color-coded visualizations with semantic meaning: gray for baselines, green for their own methods, neutral colors for human baselines.\n\n4. Prefers performance-ordered data presentation (highest to lowest, left to right).\n\n5. Prefers minimal, clean visualizations without gridlines, titles, or legends when appropriate.\n\n6. Working directory is /Users/zoraaa/Downloads/test-visual for visualization projects.\n"
          },
          "skill": {
            "awm-vs-mindact-across-transfer-settings.md": "Create Bar Chart Comparing AWM vs MindAct Performance Across Transfer Settings\n1. Document data structure and visualization design strategy (chart type, color scheme, layout)\n2. Create initial HTML visualization with D3.js grouped bar chart\n3. Convert to pure SVG implementation for better preview compatibility\n4. Adjust y-axis range from 0-50 to 20-50 to amplify visual differences\n5. Replace SVG with plain HTML/CSS implementation and increase figure size\n6. Increase all text sizes significantly and compress bar region to reduce whitespace\n7. Improve horizontal layout spacing and rotate y-axis label 90 degrees\n8. Simplify y-axis to sparse 10-step intervals (20, 30, 40, 50) and spread legend horizontally\n9. Format all x-axis labels consistently as two-line text and clean up positioning\n10. Export final HTML visualization to PNG using Selenium/Chrome\n",
            "webarena-agent-performance-trend-analysis.md": "WebArena Agent Performance Trend Analysis - Create Scatter Plot Visualization\n1. Parse and organize the raw WebArena benchmark data (31 data points from 2023-2025)\n2. Sort data chronologically and document all entries including duplicates representing different agents/methods\n3. Create initial HTML/CSS line chart visualization with all 31 data points\n4. Convert line chart to scatter plot by removing connecting line and increasing dot size\n5. Update formatting: make axis labels consistent, add y-axis title \"Success Rate (%)\", change to dark gray text, enlarge data points\n6. Export visualization to PNG format using headless Chrome\n7. Fix PNG truncation by regenerating with larger window size (1720×920 pixels)\n",
            "webarena-benchmark-success-rate-visualization.md": "WebArena Benchmark Success Rate Visualization\n1. Parse benchmark data and structure it into JSON format with systems, categories, and success rates\n2. Create initial HTML bar chart visualization with SVG rendering, orange color scheme, and interactive tooltips\n3. Update chart styling: increase text sizes (title, labels, values), reduce bar widths, change color scheme (gray for baselines, green for AWM, blue-gray for human), and reorder bars to show AWM last\n4. Reverse bar order to align with performance ranking (highest to lowest: AWM → Human → Baselines)\n5. Restore and refine collapsed figure structure, fixing HTML formatting and repositioning elements\n6. Remove title and legend, optimize container width to 700px to better fit bar regions\n7. Remove all gridlines for cleaner, minimal appearance\n8. Export final visualization as PNG image using Playwright browser automation\n"
          }
        }
