            {
              "path": "design_notes.md",
              "content": "# Mind2Web Dataset Visualization Design\n\n## Data Structure\n\n### Dataset Splits and Performance Values\n\n**Cross-Task Split:**\n- MindAct: 36.2\n- AWM-offline: 45.1\n- AWM-online: 43.6\n\n**Cross-Website Split:**\n- MindAct: 30.1\n- AWM-offline: 33.7\n- AWM-online: 33.9\n\n**Cross-Domain Split:**\n- MindAct: 26.4\n- AWM-offline: 32.6\n- AWM-online: 35.5\n\n### Data Observations\n1. **AWM superiority**: Both AWM methods consistently outperform MindAct baseline across all splits\n2. **Progressive trend**: AWM-online performance relative to AWM-offline improves as difficulty increases (cross-task → cross-website → cross-domain)\n   - Cross-task: offline (45.1) > online (43.6), difference = -1.5\n   - Cross-website: offline (33.7) < online (33.9), difference = +0.2\n   - Cross-domain: offline (32.6) < online (35.5), difference = +2.9\n\n## Visualization Strategy\n\n### Primary Insights to Communicate\n1. **Insight 1**: AWM methods (both offline and online) consistently outperform MindAct baseline\n2. **Insight 2**: AWM-online gradually outperforms AWM-offline as transfer difficulty increases\n\n### Chart Type\n**Grouped bar chart** with three groups (one per split), each containing three bars (one per method)\n\n### Layout Design\n\n**Ordering:**\n- X-axis groups: Cross-Task → Cross-Website → Cross-Domain (left to right, increasing difficulty)\n- Within each group: MindAct, AWM-offline, AWM-online (logical progression showing baseline then improvements)\n\n**Rationale**: This ordering naturally reveals the progressive trend where AWM-online catches up and surpasses AWM-offline\n\n### Color Scheme\n\nFollowing user preferences for semantic color coding:\n\n- **MindAct (baseline)**: Gray (#888888 or similar neutral gray)\n- **AWM-offline**: Medium green (#4CAF50 or #5CB85C)\n- **AWM-online**: Darker/richer green (#2E7D32 or #449944)\n\n**Rationale**:\n- Gray clearly distinguishes the baseline method\n- Two shades of green show both methods are \"ours\" while allowing distinction\n- Darker green for online helps it stand out when showing the crossover trend\n\n### Typography & Styling\n\nFollowing user preferences:\n- **Title**: 32px, bold\n- **Axis labels**: 20px\n- **Value labels**: 18px (displayed on or above bars)\n- **Bar width**: ~70px per bar\n- **Bar spacing**: Adequate grouping to show relationship within splits\n- **Minimal design**: Clean, no gridlines, simple axes\n\n### Visual Elements\n\n1. **Bars**: Grouped vertically showing performance values\n2. **Y-axis**: Performance metric (0-50 range suggested)\n3. **X-axis**: Three split categories clearly labeled\n4. **Value labels**: Display exact values on each bar for precision\n5. **Legend**: Simple, positioned top-right or top-center\n\n### Key Visual Cues\n\nTo emphasize Insight 2 (AWM-online overtaking AWM-offline):\n- Position bars so the green shades are adjacent for easy comparison\n- Consider subtle visual markers or slight emphasis on the crossover point\n- The natural height progression will visually communicate the trend\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Use D3.js for flexibility and control\n- SVG-based rendering for crisp text at all sizes\n- Responsive design to ensure readability\n- Working directory: `/Users/zoraaa/Downloads/test-visual`\n- Output file: `mind2web_results.html`\n",
              "content_source": "filesystem",
              "error": null
