          "skill": {
            "about-me-slide-creation.md": "About Me Slide Creation with Theme Variations\n1. Plan workflow for creating a personalized \"About Me\" slide\n2. Create initial HTML slide with purple gradient theme and structured content sections\n3. Iterate through color theme variations (pink, yellow, green, orange) based on user requests\n4. Generate final green-themed slide with research focus, project cards, and writing philosophy\n5. Convert slide from portrait to landscape orientation (16:9 aspect ratio)\n6. Adjust layout to 4-column grid and optimize typography for widescreen format\n7. Verify output at key milestones\n",
            "context-vs-weight-updates.md": "Writing and Refining a Research Abstract Through Iterative Editing\n1. Create workflow plan for writing abstract with structured steps\n2. Search for existing project documentation to understand research context\n3. Draft abstract outline with four main sections (problem, approach, methodology, contributions)\n4. Write complete abstract draft following the outline structure\n5. Iteratively refine abstract based on user edits to outline, incorporating:\n6. Verify changes after each major revision cycle\n",
            "create-about-me-poster-in-landscape-layout.md": "Create About Me Poster in Landscape Layout\n1. Gather user background information from memory files and compile into a profile document\n2. Create initial HTML poster in landscape format with professional styling and gradient theme\n3. Update poster to white background with black borders and remove all colors per user request\n4. Adjust layout to 4:3 aspect ratio and reduce text content by 80%\n5. Add CSS-based icons for each section and framework dimension\n6. Change aspect ratio to 16:9 landscape format (1600px × 900px)\n7. Redesign layout as three-column grid without squared blocks, using SVG icons and vertical sections\n8. Verify and fix 16:9 dimensions with proper box-sizing\n9. Add colorful styling with purple/blue gradient theme and colored accents\n10. Update entire color scheme to warm orange tones throughout the poster\n",
            "creating-a-bar-chart-visualization.md": "Creating a Bar Chart Visualization\n1. Create a workflow plan for building a bar chart with three main steps\n2. Ask user to select data type (sample data, research metrics, or custom data)\n3. Write chart specification file with data, styling, dimensions, and visual features\n4. Read the chart specification to confirm details\n5. Generate HTML bar chart file using Chart.js library\n6. Identify preview rendering issue with JavaScript-based chart\n7. Rewrite HTML file using pure SVG instead of Chart.js for better preview compatibility\n8. Verify the updated chart displays bars correctly\n",
