            "about-me-slide-creation.md": "User researches AI agents that absorb human expertise through context rather than fine-tuning.\n\nUser focuses on expertise distillation across task distribution, procedural workflow, output verification, and automation granularity.\n\nUser advocates for human-centered coding agents that enhance rather than replace developer judgment.\n\nUser prefers writing with vivid metaphors, active verbs, concise prose, smooth transitions, and clear logic.\n\nUser tests AI frameworks through writing and visual design tasks in simulated benchmarks and real-world deployment.\n\nUser compares context-based adaptation versus traditional fine-tuning for capturing expert knowledge nuance.\n",
            "context-vs-weight-updates.md": "User prefers artistic, vivid writing style with concrete metaphors and dynamic verbs over plain academic prose.\n\nThe project studies expertise distillation into AI agents via context-based vs weight-based adaptation approaches.\n\nUser wants concise writing, particularly in results sections, avoiding redundant phrases.\n\nEvaluation uses writing and visual design tasks via both simulated benchmarks and in-the-wild deployment with human experts.\n\nThe framework elicits expertise across four dimensions: task distribution, procedural workflow, output verification, and automation granularity.\n\nUser values smooth flow between sentences with explicit transitions and clear logical connections.\n",
